  "notes": [
    {
      "en": "The current package emits an extra empty `<a class=\"footnote-anchor\">` inside `<sup class=\"footnote-ref\">` so that consumers can set a CSS scroll offset, while the reference keeps the back-reference id on the link itself. Normalization removes that element and unifies the generated `footnote*` / `fn*` ids and `href`s before comparing.",
      "zh": "当前包会在 `<sup class=\"footnote-ref\">` 内额外输出一个空的 `<a class=\"footnote-anchor\">`，以便使用者设置 CSS 滚动偏移，而参考包将反向引用 id 保留在链接本身。归一化会在对比前移除该元素，并统一生成的 `footnote*` / `fn*` id 与 `href`。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Generated footnote ids, reference ids and `href` targets are normalized; footnote numbering, captions (`[1]`, `[1:1]`) and the rendered footnote list are compared.",
      "zh": "生成的脚注 id、引用 id 和 `href` 目标会被归一化；脚注编号、caption（`[1]`、`[1:1]`）以及渲染出的脚注列表仍会对比。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Neither plugin takes options, so `ourOptions` and `referenceOptions` are omitted.",
      "zh": "两个插件都不接受选项，因此省略 `ourOptions` 和 `referenceOptions`。"
    },
    {
      "en": "The current package escapes a caller-provided `env.docId` before interpolating it into generated ids (the reference does not). The harness renders without `env`, so the `docId` path is not exercised by the cases.",
      "zh": "当前包会先转义调用方提供的 `env.docId`，再将其插入生成的 id（参考包不会）。对比工具渲染时不传 `env`，因此这些用例不会覆盖 `docId` 路径。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Scaling: the reference `footnote_tail` rebuilds the token array for every footnote definition (`state.tokens = state.tokens.concat(tokens)`), which is quadratic in the number of footnotes; the current package pushes into the existing array instead. `many-footnotes` exposes this (reference exponent ~1.6, current ~1.0).",
      "zh": "扩展性：参考包的 `footnote_tail` 会为每个脚注定义重建 token 数组（`state.tokens = state.tokens.concat(tokens)`），其开销随脚注数量呈二次增长；当前包则直接向已有数组推入。`many-footnotes` 暴露了这一点（参考包拟合指数约 1.6，当前包约 1.0）。"
    },
    {
      "en": "Attribute order is normalized.",
      "zh": "属性顺序已归一化。"
    }
  ]
}
